# Agent ship discipline

Keep responses concise. Do not restate the user's question. Prefer doing the work over narrating it.

## Verification = evidence

Do not hand off with “it should work.”

- Build/lint/tests: real command, exit 0
- Tests: pass/fail counts (or note none exist)
- UI: screenshot or concrete click path when the change is visual
- Bug fix: same reproduction fails before, passes after
- URL/API: hit it yourself before asking the user to test; report status and what you checked

Bad: “Updated the code; should be fine.”  
Good: “Tests/lint exit 0. Named the files changed and how you verified.”

## Debugging: three strikes, then stop

1. First failure → note what you tried and why it failed; try a **different** approach  
2. Second → reassess whether the diagnosis is wrong  
3. Third → **stop**. Summarize the three attempts, errors, revised root cause, and a new proposal. Do not attempt a fourth fix without explicit approval  

Do not ship incremental variations of the same failed idea.

## Reproduce before you fix

Start every bug fix by watching a reproduction fail (curl, script, click steps, or query). Fix. Watch the same reproduction pass. Prefer a failing test when the area already has tests; otherwise leave a clear repro recipe in the PR/commit.

## Plans

For multi-step or multi-file work (not tiny one-file tweaks):

- Write a short plan to disk under `.cursor/plans/` (or the repo’s usual plans location): goal, approach, files, verification, open questions  
- If the user pastes a detailed plan into chat, save it to disk first before implementing  
- Before claiming done: re-read the plan, check each step, and state any gaps out loud (“plan said X; I did not do Y”), then close them  

## Dig artifacts

When a test page, route, flag, seed user, or temporary copy has served its purpose: **rename/scrub to production identity or delete it in the same change**. Do not leave “I’ll clean it before go-live.” Read user-visible strings before handoff.

## Keys and env

If a feature needs a missing secret: ask immediately (which key, which service, where it will live). Do not silently skip or fake success. Prefer documenting required vars in the repo’s env example file when adding a new integration.

## Delegation heuristic

- Delegate / fan out: “read X and tell me Y”, broad search, logs, boilerplate, doc greps, mechanical rewrites  
- Keep on the main agent: architecture, subtle cross-file bugs, planning, multi-step orchestration  

## Session hygiene

- Prefer not re-reading unchanged files already loaded this session (re-read if the file may have been edited)  
- After a multi-step or debugging session, you may offer one line: `pattern worth remembering: …` — only write durable gotchas into `AGENTS.md` when the user agrees  
- Never save session-only state, speculative one-off guesses, or things the user said not to remember  

## Already required for this repo

Also follow `AGENTS.md` for stack-specific setup, lint/test commands, and project gotchas.

